{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, researchers discovered simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, causing kinetic mismatch that worsens moisture damage. The team designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, optimize energy alignment, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record ambient flexible efficiencies of 24.84% (0.09 cm²) and 21.46% on mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000 h damp aging at 85 ± 5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture damage",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, optimizes energy alignment, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to resolve kinetic-environmental coupling in scalable flexible photovoltaics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei, profiling four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization. The resulting atlas identified 100+ cell subclasses and defined active, primed, and repressive chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 define repressive states. This resource enables deep learning models for predicting cell-type-specific epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The atlas spans over 100 brain cell subclasses using integrated epigenomic profiling",
    "Active chromatin states marked by combinatorial histone modifications better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct modes of cell-type-specific gene repression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This multimodal epigenomic atlas provides a comprehensive framework for annotating the brain regulatory genome and interpreting non-coding disease risk variants through cell-type-specific epigenomic features."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how early human settlement in the Arabian desert was influenced by stone availability for tool production, beyond water resources. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Rub' al Khali, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable materials in 55 of 125 locations with palaeolake deposits, despite abundant water. Spatial analysis indicates settlement required co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, with raw-material availability improving site discrimination by 0.695–0.768. This suggests stone availability independently constrained early human dispersal into deserts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials were found in 55 of 125 locations with palaeolake deposits",
    "Spatial modeling shows settlement required co-occurrence of water and lithic resources",
    "Raw-material availability improved site discrimination by 0.695–0.768"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that stone availability for tool production independently constrained early human dispersal into arid regions, challenging models that prioritize water availability alone."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and inflammation in the gut. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Prostaglandin activates PKA to upregulate tissue-protective factors in ILC3s",
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (e.g., PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "IL-23 overproduction reduces PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, demonstrating how IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation contributes to gut inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a novel behavioral change framework by testing its efficacy in real-world settings. The approach involved applying the paradigm to diverse populations and measuring outcomes against established benchmarks. Results indicate significant improvements in target behaviors compared to conventional methods, suggesting potential for scalable interventions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The paradigm demonstrates measurable behavioral improvements",
    "Real-world application shows higher efficacy than traditional approaches",
    "The framework offers a scalable solution for behavior change interventions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances behavioral science by providing a validated, scalable paradigm for effective behavior change, contributing to the development of evidence-based public health strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of fabricating nanocomposites with high nanofiller loadings and ordered nanostructures using additive manufacturing. It introduces shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing, which aligns nanomaterials like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes under high shear forces. The method enables scalable production of complex 3D architectures with high filler loadings (up to 55 wt% BN in polylactic acid). Post-sintering yields materials with zero volume shrinkage, exceptional thermomechanical stability, and tailored thermal properties: vertically aligned composites show enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K), horizontally aligned structures provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K), and BN membranes achieve compressive strength of 3.4 MPa.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing aligns high-loading nanomaterials (e.g., 55 wt% boron nitride in polylactic acid) under shear forces",
    "Post-sintered composites exhibit zero volume shrinkage and thermomechanical stability up to polymer decomposition temperatures",
    "Tailored thermal properties: vertically aligned BN composites have high thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K), horizontally aligned structures offer thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K), and BN membranes show compressive strength of 3.4 MPa"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach enables scalable fabrication of nanocomposites with high nanofiller loadings and long-range ordered nanostructures, bridging nanoscale functionalities and macroscale geometries for applications in thermal management and structural materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used computational simulations of the Drosophila ventral nerve cord connectomes to identify a central pattern generator (CPG) for fly walking. By screening descending neurons, researchers pinpointed DNg100 as a key command neuron driving rhythmic leg movements. Simulations revealed a minimal three-neuron circuit—comprising one inhibitory and two excitatory interneurons—that generates coordinated leg rhythms across all six legs and is necessary and sufficient for rhythmic output. The work also confirmed a separate descending pathway (DNb08) using optogenetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "DNg100 acts as the primary command neuron initiating rhythmic leg movements in walking flies",
    "A minimal three-neuron circuit (one inhibitory, two excitatory interneurons) generates rhythmic leg rhythms across all six legs",
    "Optogenetic validation confirmed the role of descending pathway DNb08 in rhythmic leg movements"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research identifies the cellular and synaptic architecture of a functional CPG circuit for fly walking, providing a foundational model for understanding rhythmic motor control in insects and potential evolutionary conservation across species."
}

{
  "summary": "This study provides the earliest direct evidence of cannabis consumption, dating to at least 2800 years ago, through ancient human hair from a Siberian tomb. The analysis identified psychoactive compounds, indicating use for recreational purposes across Eurasia. The findings establish cannabis use in prehistoric times, challenging assumptions about its historical adoption and informing modern discussions on its medical, public health, and societal implications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of psychoactive cannabis compounds in ancient human hair from a Siberian tomb",
    "Cannabis use dates back at least  2800 years",
    "The practice was used for psychoactive purposes across Eurasia"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research establishes cannabis consumption in prehistoric Eurasia, providing the earliest direct evidence of its psychoactive use and expanding historical understanding of human drug utilization."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility between cocatalysts in alkaline and pure water systems as a critical bottleneck. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieves 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric water splitting at 420 nm",
    "Enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over nitride materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing water-splitting photocatalysts."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a 4-day high-fat diet (HFD) exposure at disease onset exacerbates inflammation comparably to chronic obesity. The effect is time-sensitive, requiring HFD within a specific 4-day window. Neutrophil recruitment, NLRP3 activation, and IL-1β production drive this amplification, which persists post-recovery as chromatin-poised T cells. Switching to low-fat diet during the same window reverses exacerbation. These findings demonstrate that transient dietary states during inflammation can durably reprogram immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure at disease onset exacerbates skin inflammation in lean mice to levels comparable with chronic obesity",
    "The inflammatory effect is restricted to a 4-day window post-inflammation initiation; HFD outside this window has no impact",
    "Neutrophil-mediated NLRP3-IL-1β signaling licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, with persistent chromatin-poised T cells after recovery"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that short-lived dietary states during acute inflammation can durably reprogram tissue immune memory through neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β pathways, revealing a temporal window for dietary interventions to modulate inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates cost-effective fabrication of fatigue-resistant elastocaloric cooling (eC) refrigerants using shape memory alloys (SMAs). The research employs a 'stamping and stacking' method to create porous nitinol (NiTi) structures with enhanced heat transfer and mechanical stability. The approach achieves >108 compression cycles and 3850 W/kg specific cooling power while reducing production costs by one order of magnitude compared to conventional methods.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Stacked porous NiTi structures withstand >108 compression cycles without failure",
    "The method delivers high specific cooling power of .3850 W/kg",
    "Fabrication costs are reduced by one order of magnitude using stamping and stacking"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a scalable manufacturing technique for fatigue-resistant elastocaloric cooling refrigerants, advancing practical implementation of eco-friendly thermoelectric cooling systems through cost-effective structural design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates stabilizing ruthenium sites in acidic oxygen evolution reactions (OER) by engineering Nb-doped Ru/RuO2 heterostructures to suppress lattice oxygen mechanism (LOM)-driven dissolution. The approach combines Nb doping with Ru/RuO2 interfaces to enhance deprotonation and oxygen intermediate adsorption while stabilizing lattice oxygen. Results show a catalyst achieving 186 mV overpotential at 10 mA cm-2 with 3000-hour durability in PEMWE systems, breaking the activity-stability trade-off.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Nb-doped Ru/RuO2 heterostructure inhibits LOM-induced Ru dissolution",
    "Enhanced deprotonation capability and oxygen intermediate adsorption improve catalytic activity",
    "3000-hour durability at 10 mA cm-2 in PEMWE systems"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a design strategy for stable, high-activity OER catalysts by decoupling activity and stability through lattice oxygen stabilization, advancing proton exchange membrane water electrolysis technology."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of starlight suppression in exoplanet imaging by developing a physics-based method that models and compensates for telescope instabilities. Using automatic differentiation, the approach optimizes millions of parameters to achieve sensitivity 2-15 times better than standard techniques. It successfully detected 51 Eridani b with JWST data, demonstrating improved performance for future exoplanet observatories.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The method achieves 2-15 times higher sensitivity than standard starlight subtraction techniques",
    "First detection of 51 Eridanib at 4.3 μm using JWST NIRCam coronagraph data",
    "Framework applicable to future observatories like Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope and Habitable Worlds Observatory"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a physics-based framework for compensating telescope instabilities in exoplanet imaging, significantly enhancing sensitivity for direct detection of faint exoplanets beyond 1 AU."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether GLP-1 receptor agonist therapies influence cancer incidence. Using observational data from clinical trials and registries, it assessed cancer risk patterns across diverse populations. The analysis found no significant association between GLP-1 therapy and increased cancer risk, suggesting these treatments may not elevate cancer susceptibility.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No significant increase in cancer incidence observed among GLP-1 receptor agonist users",
    "Cancer risk patterns remained stable across different demographic groups",
    "GLP-1 therapies do not appear to elevate cancer susceptibility based on current evidence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings provide reassurance that GLP-1 receptor agonist therapies do not pose a heightened cancer risk, contributing to safer metabolic treatment strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a precursor-level design principle for hard-carbon anodes in sodium-ion batteries by regulating asphaltene molecular heterogeneity through cohesion-solvation mechanisms. Toluene-fractionated precursors undergo oxidative crosslinking to form turbostratic domains and closed pores. The developed hard-carbon performance index (HPSI) and density functional theory (DFT) analysis reveal enhanced sodium affinity and lower migration barriers. The AHC-80-1400 hard-carbon achieves 400.1 mAh g-1 at 0.05 A g-1 with 87.7% initial capacity retention and 92.3% capacity retention after 10,000 cycles, demonstrating robust electrochemical performance across temperatures and scalability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Toluene-fractionated asphaltene precursors undergo oxidative crosslinking to form turbostratic domains and closed pores",
    "The AHC-80-1400 hard-carbon achieves 400.1 mAh g-1 at 0.05 A g-1 with 87.7% initial capacity retention",
    "DFT analysis indicates stronger sodium affinity and lower migration barriers in defect-engineered carbon galleries"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a precursor-stage molecular selection strategy to control hard-carbon structural evolution, enabling high-performance sodium-ion battery anodes through feedstock heterogeneity regulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines indoor photovoltaic (PV) technologies, including perovskite, organic, amorphous-silicon, III-V, and dye-sensitized types, to address bottlenecks in low-light operation and scaling. It identifies that wide-bandgap absorbers and reduced non-radiative voltage losses enhance performance, while lower series resistance improves geometric fill factor and reduces interconnections. Shunt pathways and leakage consume weak photocurrents. The study emphasizes transparent benchmarking practices and links device performance to manufacturability, regulatory constraints, and product integration for real-world deployment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Wide-bandgap absorbers and reduced non-radiative voltage losses improve low-light performance",
    "Lower series resistance enables wider subcells and fewer interconnections, increasing geometric fill factor",
    "Shunt pathways and leakage pathways consume more of the weak photocurrent under low-light conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes critical design principles for indoor PVs that bridge laboratory performance with scalable, real-world deployment under low-light conditions, advancing the transition from prototypes to practical energy-harvesting solutions for distributed electronics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines the U.S. federal policy framework concerning archaeological protections, focusing on legislative efforts to undermine the National Historic Preservation Act's preproject review requirements. The research identifies potential threats to archaeological preservation through congressional and executive actions targeting regulatory compliance. Findings indicate that weakening these legal safeguards could significantly increase risks to cultural heritage sites without adequate mitigation strategies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Congressional initiatives aim to reduce preproject review mandates for archaeological projects",
    "Executive actions target regulatory compliance mechanisms under the National Historic Preservation Act",
    "Weakening these safeguards may heighten risks to cultural heritage sites without sufficient mitigation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work highlights critical vulnerabilities in federal cultural heritage protection systems under current policy shifts, contributing to understanding how legislative and executive actions impact archaeological preservation frameworks."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing tin-based perovskite solar cell performance by modifying PEDOT:PSS with a p-type small molecule, FEG. Using solid-state NMR, the researchers elucidated intermolecular interactions that redistribute PEDOT:PSS microstructure, improve charge delocalization, and reduce defects. The modified HTL enables high-quality perovskite films with larger grains and lower defect density, achieving record efficiencies of 14.92% for 1-cm² devices and 17.02% for 0.04-cm² devices while maintaining stability over 85% after 1100 h.",
  "key_findings": [
    "FEG modification of PEDOT:PSS redistributes microstructure and enhances charge delocalization",
    "Improved perovskite film quality with larger grains and reduced defect density",
    "Record efficiencies of 14.92% (1-cm²) and 17.02% (0.04-cm²) with enhanced stability"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that targeted molecular engineering of hole transport layers can significantly improve the efficiency and stability of tin-based perovskite solar cells through optimized intermolecular interactions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the deep Earth processes driving the Great Unconformity, a globally significant erosional surface preceding the Cambrian explosion. Using mantle convection models, the authors demonstrate that long-wavelength dynamic topography caused continental-scale uplift during the Cryogenian and subsequent subsidence in the Phanerozoic. These tectonic motions explain the Great Unconformity's formation and preservation, linking deep Earth dynamics to surface geological features.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Mantle convection-driven dynamic topography caused Cryogenian continental uplift",
    "Predicted prolonged Neoproterozoic uplift and Phanerozoic subsidence across Laurentia, Baltica, and North China",
    "The vertical motion scenario explains the Great Unconformity's preservation and formation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a direct link between mantle convection and the formation of the Great Unconformity, providing a deep Earth mechanism for a major surface geological feature."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether AI could solve a long-standing problem in computer science: the NP-completeness of the traveling salesman problem. Using advanced AI techniques, researchers demonstrated an AI system capable of finding optimal solutions for large-scale instances. The findings suggest AI may surpass traditional computational methods for certain complex optimization problems, potentially reshaping approaches to NP-complete problems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AI system solved large-scale traveling salesman problem instances previously considered intractable",
    "The solution approach outperformed conventional computational methods for NP-complete problems",
    "The work raises ethical questions about AI-generated research outputs and intellectual property"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research demonstrates AI's potential to solve previously intractable computational problems, advancing understanding of optimization techniques for NP-complete problems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic bottlenecks in alkaline all-iron redox flow batteries (AIRFBs) by identifying sluggish outer-sphere electron-transfer kinetics in Fe-chelate anolytes. Using Lewis-basic sulfide interfaces like Ni3S4, the research enhances electron-transfer efficiency, achieving 80.65% energy efficiency and 501.2 mW cm-2 peak power density at 200 mA cm-2, while maintaining stability over 3000 cycles.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Lewis-basic sulfide interfaces accelerate Fe-chelate anolyte redox kinetics via sulfide-assisted outer-sphere electron-transfer",
    "Ni3S4-modified electrodes achieve 80.65% energy efficiency and 501.2 mW cm-2 peak power density at 200 mA cm-2",
    "The system maintains 99.9% Coulombic efficiency and stable operation over 3000 cycles at 200 mA cm-2"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes Lewis-basic interface engineering as a general strategy to overcome kinetic limitations in alkaline redox flow batteries, enabling high power density and long-duration energy storage with earth-abundant materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used ancient genomic sequencing of 712 individuals alongside 4,092 published genomes to trace Germanic language origins. It identified a population migrating into Sweden from the Baltic region by 4000 BP, which spread across Scandinavia by 3500 BP. The research links this group to Germanic language introduction in Scandinavia 800 years earlier than previously thought, with subsequent migrations shaping the language's divergence into modern descendants.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A Baltic-origin population entered Sweden by 4000 BP, spreading across Scandinavia by 3500 BP",
    "Germanic language introduction to Scandinavia occurred 800 years earlier than traditionally assumed",
    "Post-Iron Age migrations from southern Scandinavia into Celtic-speaking regions and a northward back-migration into Denmark/Sweden coincided with Old Norse emergence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides genomic evidence for multiple migration waves that shaped the historical and linguistic development of Germanic languages across northwest Europe."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated achieving the lowest temperature ever recorded using a nested atom trap configuration. The researchers created a Bose-Einstein condensate by sequentially trapping atoms in multiple nested potential wells, mimicking Russian dolls. The approach enabled unprecedented cooling to a record-setting temperature, demonstrating a novel method for ultra-cold quantum states.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Record-setting temperature achieved via nested atom traps",
    "Bose-Einstein condensate formation in a multi-stage trapping system",
    "Novel cooling mechanism enabling ultra-cold quantum states"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances quantum cooling techniques by establishing a scalable method for generating exceptionally low temperatures in Bose-Einstein condensates."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of deep-seated osteomyelitis by developing programmable engineered living vehicles (ELVs) that autonomously navigate infected sites. ELVs, based on self-propelled E. coli Nissle 1917, integrate environmental biosensors and logic-gated computing modules to produce bacteriolytic lysostaphin and vasoactive intestinal peptide at temperatures ≥37°C. These ELVs penetrate biofilms, clear MRSA infections more effectively than vancomycin, and accelerate bone regeneration through localized microenvironment reprogramming in a rat model.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ELVs autonomously navigate to infected niches and penetrate biofilms in rat osteomyelitis models",
    "ELVs produce lysostaphin and VIP at ≥37°C to target MRSA and stimulate bone repair",
    "ELVs outperform vancomycin in pathogen clearance and accelerate bone regeneration"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a programmable living vehicle platform that synergistically combines biofilm penetration, targeted antimicrobial action, and bone regeneration for complex infections, advancing smart therapeutics through synthetic biology and micro-engineering integration."
}
